{
  "schema": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "The ten parameters for each of the twelve archetypes, extracted from archetypes.py",
    "so a run can be re-parameterised without editing code. The prose personas stay in",
    "archetypes.py: this file holds only the numbers the harnesses read.",
    "",
    "Every value is a float in [0, 1]. All twelve ids and all ten keys must be present \u2014",
    "archetypes.py raises on a missing or out-of-range value rather than filling a default,",
    "because a silently-defaulted parameter would show up as a real finding in the report.",
    "",
    "These numbers are heuristic_bots.py's inputs, and heuristic_bots.py is explicit that",
    "its parameter-to-decision mapping is one implementer's modeling choice, not ground",
    "truth. Changing a value changes what that model does; it does not change what a person",
    "with that temperament would do. See archetypes_v1.md for what each parameter means.",
    "",
    "To try different values for one run without committing them, use the",
    "archetype_overrides input on the structural workflow, or set LODGE_ARCHETYPE_OVERRIDES",
    "to a JSON object (or a path to one) shaped like {\"A03\": {\"trust\": 0.8}}."
  ],
